# Translation correlations and local cancellation

Formalization of the section "Translation correlations and local cancellation" of the blueprint
(labels `ann:sequence`, `ann:extract`, `ann:spectral`, `ann:polynomials`, `ann:factor`,
`ann:form`, `ann:invariance`, `ann:fibers`, `ann:selectors`, `ann:atomic-rigidity`,
`ann:displacement`, `ann:local`).

## Design choices

* An admissible sequence (`ann:sequence`) is a pair `(R, f)` with `R : ℕ → ℝ` and
  `f : Fin 3 → ℕ → ℝ² → ℂ` (`f j n = f_{j,n}`), see `Auto.IsAdmissibleSeq`; the box `Q` is
  any set (bounded where the theorems need it).  The translates are `Auto.annT`.
* Weak-* convergence is `Auto.annWeakStar`: convergence of the integrals against every `L¹`
  test function.
* A subsequence is a strictly monotone `φ : ℕ → ℕ`; the later lemmas are stated for the
  re-indexed sequence `(R ∘ φ, f ∘ φ)` and take as hypothesis the conclusions of the earlier
  lemmas, bundled in `Auto.aux_IsCorrelationLimits` (`ann:extract`),
  `Auto.aux_IsSpectralKernels` (`ann:spectral`) and `Auto.aux_IsLimitForm` (`ann:form`).
  The two-point limits are `k j z s t = k_j(z;s,t)` and the three-point limits are
  `h3 p s = h(p;s_0,s_1,s_2)`.
* Measurable kernels (`ext:kernel-definition`) are `Auto.IsMeasurableKernel` (Section 2).
* Trigonometric polynomials (`ann:polynomials`) are given by their finitely supported
  coefficient families `c : ℝ² →₀ ℂ`; a finite sum of elementary tensors of trigonometric
  polynomials is the same as a finite linear combination of the tensors `e_s ⊗ e_t`, and is given
  by its coefficients `c : ℝ² × ℝ² →₀ ℂ`.
* The bilinear forms `ℓ_p` are raw maps `(ℝ² → ℂ) → (ℝ² × ℝ² → ℂ) → ℂ`; their bilinearity and
  the Cauchy–Schwarz bound on `L²(ν₀) × L²(ν₁ ⊗ ν₂)` are `Auto.aux_IsBoundedBilinear`.
-/

